### Code Review finding on PR #97

Runtime diagnosis / reasoning fix is evidence-backed and CI run #356 is green, but merge is blocked by one cache-contract issue found in review:

`story.reasoning_effort` now changes the actual LM Studio request, yet `story_cache_key()` does not include the effective reasoning mode. A generation after changing `low/medium/...` to `none` can therefore reuse an older normalized Story cache entry without issuing a new request, and cached provider audit may describe a different request contract than the active config.

Requested minimal fix on the same PR branch:

- include effective reasoning mode in Story cache identity;
- invalidate/bump the pre-VID-24 request contract as needed;
- regression test that same snapshot/provider/model with different reasoning modes cannot share cached generation;
- preserve existing force/cache behavior, VID-13 preflight, strict schema, cleanup and fail-closed semantics.

VID-30 remains separate and blocked by VID-24; do not fold mandatory-segment semantic retry into PR #97.
